-# Locals:
-#   problem — a symbol from EntriesController
-#   message — Dreamwidth's own words, for :invalid
-#   form    — the entry form, if this is the Write page (its own errors are listed too)
-#
-# Shown just after the h1, and the fields point at it with aria-describedby.
- if problem == :key_rejected
  = render "journal/shared/key_failed", connection: @connection, manage_link: true
- elsif problem || form&.errors&.any?
  .flash.flash--alert.journal-notice#entry-problem{tabindex: "-1"}
    - case problem
    - when :invalid
      %p Dreamwidth didn't post it, and said: “#{message}”
      %p Your writing is still here.
    - when :timed_out
      %p
        Dreamwidth didn't answer in time, so it isn't clear whether your entry was
        posted. Your writing is still here.
      %p
        Before posting again,
        = link_to journal_dw_entries_path(@connection), target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" do
          check #{@connection.username}'s entries (opens in a new tab)
        so it isn't posted twice.
    - when :unavailable
      %p
        Couldn't reach Dreamwidth just now, so nothing was posted. Your writing is
        still here: try again in a few minutes.
    - when :journal_gone
      %p
        Dreamwidth doesn't have a journal called
        %strong= @connection.username
        any more.
    - when :entry_gone
      %p Dreamwidth doesn't have that entry. It may have been deleted.
    - if form
      - form.errors.full_messages.each do |error_message|
        %p= error_message
